NNAAMMEE
     sslleeeepp — suspend execution for an interval of time

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sslleeeepp _s_e_c_o_n_d_s

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sslleeeepp utility suspends execution for at least the given number of
     _s_e_c_o_n_d_s.  _s_e_c_o_n_d_s must be a non-negative decimal value and may contain a
     fraction.

AASSYYNNCCHHRROONNOOUUSS EEVVEENNTTSS
     SIGALRM     Terminate early, with a zero exit status.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The sslleeeepp utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Wait five seconds before running a command:

           $ sleep 5; echo Hello, World!

     List a file twice per second:

           while ls -l file; do
                   sleep 0.5
           done

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     at(1)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The sslleeeepp utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.

     Support for fractional _s_e_c_o_n_d_s is an extension to that specification.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A sslleeeepp utility first appeared in Version 4 AT&T UNIX.

     This implementation of sslleeeepp first appeared in 4.3BSD-Tahoe.

